<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Hasan-Jalalyan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hasan-Jalalyans, Hasan-Jalalyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hasan-Jalalyans were an Armenian princely family of Khachen in Artsakh, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-jalal-dawla">Hasan-Jalal Dawla</a>, who ruled in the 13th century. After his execution by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1261 the family survived as local lords, and under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> they held the melikdom of Khachen. Members of the family held the office of Catholicos of Aghvank at Gandzasar for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-hasan-jalalyan.jpg" alt="House of Hasan-Jalalyan" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Հայկ Ափրիկյան · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hasan-Jalalians.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
